<article class="env-definition" id="04AA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04AA">Definition <span data-tag="04AA">83.8.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme and $B$ an algebraic space over $S$. Let $j : R \to U \times _ B U$ be a pre-relation. Let $\phi : U \to X$ be an $R$-invariant morphism. Denote $\phi ' = \phi \circ s = \phi \circ t : R \to X$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We denote $(\phi _*\mathcal{O}_ U)^ R$ the $\mathcal{O}_ X$-sub-algebra of $\phi _*\mathcal{O}_ U$ which is the equalizer of the two maps 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \phi _*\mathcal{O}_ U \ar@<1ex>[rr]^{\phi _*s^\sharp } \ar@<-1ex>[rr]_{\phi _*t^\sharp } &  &  \phi '_*\mathcal{O}_ R }  \]
</div>
<p>
 on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$. We sometimes call this the <em>sheaf of $R$-invariant functions on $X$</em>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say <em>the functions on $X$ are the $R$-invariant functions on $U$</em> if the natural map $\mathcal{O}_ X \to (\phi _*\mathcal{O}_ U)^ R$ is an isomorphism. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>